Altype (formerly 2Talker)
Code: MIT License (see LICENSE). Parts of it come from the Language Tutor panel
(https://github.com/ikstro/cc-translator), MIT License, same author.

Translator (vendor/bergamot, shipped; models downloaded on first use from Mozilla's servers)
  Firefox Translations by Mozilla: the Bergamot translator built to WebAssembly
  (https://github.com/mozilla/translations) and its loader from Firefox
  (toolkit/components/translations, https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox),
  Mozilla Public License 2.0 (https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/). The files are shipped unmodified;
  their source is at the links above. The translation models are Mozilla's, under the same license.

Word dictionary (media/dict/*.json; other languages downloaded from the cc-translator dict-1 release)
  Built from WikDict (https://www.wikdict.com) by Karl Bartel,
  data from Wiktionary (https://www.wiktionary.org) via DBnary,
  licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike License
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
  The dictionary files are a derived work and are shared under the same license.

Icons: @vscode/codicons, Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (fonts) / MIT (code).

Common words (media/common-en.txt: the 3000 most frequent English words, for the dotted line under the others;
media/layout/{en,ru,uk}.txt: the most frequent English, Russian and Ukrainian words, which tell the keyboard layout a word was meant for;
media/lang-words.json: the 200 most frequent words of 25 languages, which tell the language of a text)
  From FrequencyWords by Hermit Dave (https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords), counted over
  the OpenSubtitles 2018 corpus (https://opus.nlpl.eu/OpenSubtitles.php), Creative Commons
  Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The lists are a
  derived work and are shared under the same license.

Natural voice (downloaded on request from the cc-translator voice-1 release, not shipped)
  Kokoro-82M by hexgrad (https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M), Apache License 2.0;
    ONNX export by onnx-community. Text rules in src/kokoro.ts follow kokoro-js (Apache License 2.0).
  ONNX Runtime by Microsoft (https://onnxruntime.ai), MIT License; Altype bundles the
    JavaScript of onnxruntime-node and downloads its native library.
  phonemizer.js by Xenova (https://github.com/xenova/phonemizer.js), Apache License 2.0, which
    contains eSpeak NG (https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng), GNU General Public License v3.0.
    It runs as a separate file in the voice process; its source is at the links above.

Electron (https://www.electronjs.org), MIT License; Chromium and Node.js under their own licenses
(see LICENSES.chromium.html in the installed app). koffi by Niels Martignène, MIT License.

Fonts (media/fonts, shipped): Inter by Rasmus Andersson (https://rsms.me/inter) and JetBrains Mono by
JetBrains (https://www.jetbrains.com/lp/mono/), both under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
(https://openfontlicense.org); the files are the Latin and Cyrillic subsets from Fontsource.
